  25:     """
  26:     Slide the non-square sprite to the square anchor and replace the anchor with the sprite's mirror image.
  27: 
  28:     Input structure:
  29:     - The background is the most common color.
  30:     - There is one 8-connected non-background sprite that is not a solid 2x2 square.
  31:     - There is one solid 2x2 square anchor in another non-background color.
  32: 
  33:     Rule:
  34:     - Move the sprite straight toward the anchor along their unique cardinal separation until it touches the anchor's near edge.
  35:     - Reflect the moved sprite across that near edge and draw the reflected copy in the anchor color.
  36:     - Clear the original locations; the output keeps only the moved sprite and reflected anchor-color copy.
